 "subgroup_explanation": "The three values use the same set: all 2,810 SemEval test pairs with the 289 self pairs kept and unresolvable pairs counted as not listed, pooled AUROC of the 0/1 lookup, sentence bootstrap (Amendment 7 experiment 5). Both subgroups beat the pooled value because co-mention is associated with both the label and the score (Simpson's paradox). Co-mentioned pairs are rarely positive (54 of 1023, 0.053) but are listed often (FPR 0.724); not co-mentioned pairs are positive more often (0.177) and listed less (FPR 0.617). Pooling weights the TPR by where the positives are (0.854 of positives are not co-mentioned, so pooled TPR 0.709 sits near the low subgroup TPR 0.675) and the FPR by where the negatives are (0.397 of negatives are co-mentioned, which pulls pooled FPR up to 0.660). The pooled TPR minus FPR, 0.049, is smaller than in either subgroup (0.183 and 0.058), so 0.5 (1 + TPR - FPR) is 0.525 overall against 0.591 and 0.529.",
